{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and","id":1204985,"title":"I\u2019m homebrewing for a Beast campaign, and....","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-09T15:11:40-07:00","id":1204985,"title":"I\u2019m homebrewing for a Beast campaign, and....","content":"I\u2019ve been looking through my various corebooks, but none of the established cities really catch my interest. I thought about my own area, but it is definitely <i>not</i> an ideal location for hidden supernatural beings and occult shenanigans. And just randomly searching for cities is basically just me stabbing in the dark.<br /> <br /> So...I\u2019d like some suggestions of where to start. The following qualifications <i>must</i> be adhered to:<br /> 1.It must be somewhere in the US. (Alaska and Hawaii are fine, however, despite not being in the continental US.)<br /> 2.It must have a sizeable mundane population for supernatural beings to hide within, or else a s***ton of wilderness to lurk within.<br /> 3.It cannot be from any nWoD/CofD corebooks or sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, thanks for any replies! I know this, itself, is a shot in the dark, but, hey!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 04-09-2018, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T15:30:02-07:00","id":1204989,"title":"","content":"Try Portland, Oregon. It's a big city surrounded by deep, dense forests, and there's tons of Bigfoot sightings from that area. Afaik it's not used as a setting in any of the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T15:43:02-07:00","id":1204992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1204989#post1204989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try Portland, Oregon. It's a big city surrounded by deep, dense forests, and there's tons of Bigfoot sightings from that area. Afaik it's not used as a setting in any of the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Definitely a lot of Beast-style mythology there, centered around Bigfoot and Bigfoot-sightings. Aside from Bigfoot, though, what other Portland cryptocritters are there in local folklore? Anything from the tribes that once lived in the area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T15:45:02-07:00","id":1204993,"title":"","content":"Plus, I\u2019m going to keep crossover explicitly in mind, as this is a Beast game. True, 90% of the focus will be on the Begotten...but, still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T16:11:22-07:00","id":1205002,"title":"","content":"Newark, Ohio (Population: 49K+, Strangeness: Earthworks)<br /> Homestead, Florida (Population: 68K+, Strangeness: Coral Castle)<br /> Roanoke Island (Population: 6K+ (though nearby Virginia is more populated), Strangeness: Entire colony disappeared)<br /> Roswell, New Mexico (Population: 48K+, Strangeness: Area 51/Aliens)<br /> Branson, Missouri (Population: <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">14K+ (+Tourists), Strangeness: &quot;Christian Vegas&quot;)<br /> <br /> Baltimore, Maryland (Population: 2M+, Reason: High crime (at least in public perception) leads to fear)<br /> Providence, Rhode Island (Population: 179K+, Reason: H.P. Lovecraft's home - Makara)<br /> Salem, Massachusetts (Population: 43K+, Reason: Salem Witch Trials - old fear, and Mage-Kinship opportunities)<br /> Atlanta, Georgia (Population: 4.9M+, Reason: Race Riots - lots of fear, some still lingering)</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T16:25:00-07:00","id":1205006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1205002#post1205002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Newark, Ohio (Population: 49K+, Strangeness: Earthworks)<br /> Homestead, Florida (Population: 68K+, Strangeness: Coral Castle)<br /> Roanoke Island (Population: 6K+ (though nearby Virginia is more populated), Strangeness: Entire colony disappeared)<br /> Roswell, New Mexico (Population: 48K+, Strangeness: Area 51/Aliens)<br /> Branson, Missouri (Population: <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">14K+ (+Tourists), Strangeness: &amp;quot;Christian Vegas&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Baltimore, Maryland (Population: 2M+, Reason: High crime (at least in public perception) leads to fear)<br /> Providence, Rhode Island (Population: 179K+, Reason: H.P. Lovecraft's home - Makara)<br /> Salem, Massachusetts (Population: 43K+, Reason: Salem Witch Trials - old fear, and Mage-Kinship opportunities)<br /> Atlanta, Georgia (Population: 4.9M+, Reason: Race Riots - lots of fear, some still lingering)</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Bless you, sir! This is <i>exactly</i> what I\u2019m looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T16:36:13-07:00","id":1205007,"title":"","content":"I will also second Branson because that place is <i>weird. </i>(And I say it as a lifelong Missourian.) It's sort of tucked away in the Ozark Mountains just south of Springfield, but there's a massive theme park, miles of country-western shows, and televangelists Jim and Tammy Faye Bakker at one point owned about half the town.<br /> <br /> As a bonus, if the Ozarks aren't spooky enough on their own, it's about an hour-ish drive from the Oklahoma border and the <a href=\"https://www.joplinmo.org/575/The-Spook-Light\" target=\"_blank\">Joplin Spook Light</a>.<br /> <br /> I myself have been working on Champaign-Urbana, IL as a Demon setting (combine population 120,000, weirdness: lots) but I haven't focused on much outside the God-Machine yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T17:49:23-07:00","id":1205025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1205007#post1205007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will also second Branson because that place is <i>weird. </i>(And I say it as a lifelong Missourian.) It's sort of tucked away in the Ozark Mountains just south of Springfield, but there's a massive theme park, miles of country-western shows, and televangelists Jim and Tammy Faye Bakker at one point owned about half the town.<br /> <br /> As a bonus, if the Ozarks aren't spooky enough on their own, it's about an hour-ish drive from the Oklahoma border and the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.joplinmo.org/575/The-Spook-Light&amp;quot;]Joplin</a> Spook Light[/URL].<br /> <br /> I myself have been working on Champaign-Urbana, IL as a Demon setting (combine population 120,000, weirdness: lots) but I haven't focused on much outside the God-Machine yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm...interesting! The \u201cChristian Vegas\u201d certainly has a ring to it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T18:29:49-07:00","id":1205037,"title":"","content":"Hmmm....lets\u2019 see what we have, so far:<br /> Atlanta, Georgia. I think I\u2019ll skip this one.<br /> Baltimore, Maryland. High crime rate\u2014-excellent cover for various supernatural feuds.<br /> Branson, Missouri. \u201cThe Christian Vegas\u201d. The very idea is intriguing. Religion can easily lead to good feeding-grounds for Beasts, and the gaudieness of it all is certainly appealing.<br /> Portland, Oregon. BIGFOOT!<br /> Providence, Rhode Island. Eh. I\u2019ll stay away from this one.<br /> Roanoke, Virginia. Maybe the entire colony got swallowed up into the Primordial Dream!<br /> Roswell, New Mexico. Eh. I\u2019m staying away from this one.<br /> Salem, Massachusetts. Already covered by Mummy and Mage, if I recall correctly.<br /> <br /> A pair of questions, though:<br /> What are these \u201cearthworks\u201d in Newark, Ohio? Are we talking Mound Builder stuff?<br /> What is this \u201ccoral castle\u201d in Homestead, Florida?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T18:45:16-07:00","id":1205040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1205037#post1205037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is this \u201ccoral castle\u201d in Homestead, Florida?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically what it sounds like, though it would be more of a fort or outpost than a castle, as I think it only housed one person. It's more of a sad story than a spooky one but apparently people do attribute supernatural stuff to it. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_Castle\" target=\"_blank\">Tourist trap</a> seems an appropriate name.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://rvca738f6h5tbwmj3mxylox3-wpengine.netdna-ssl.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/Alamy_EAT87Y_CoralCastle.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://www.stephensills.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/07/img_1652.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-09-2018, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T18:55:44-07:00","id":1205042,"title":"","content":"Sad story? Do tell!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T03:17:07-07:00","id":1205128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_Castle\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/12/Coral_Castle_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_Castle\" target=\"_blank\"> Coral Castle - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_Castle\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_Castle </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newark_Earthworks\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Newark_Earthworks_Wall_and_Moat.jpg/1280px-Newark_Earthworks_Wall_and_Moat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newark_Earthworks\" target=\"_blank\"> Newark Earthworks - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newark_Earthworks\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newark_Earthworks </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-10-2018, 06:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T06:01:17-07:00","id":1205156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1205128#post1205128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_Castle\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_Castle</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newark_Earthworks\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newark_Earthworks</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, i just read both articles, and...<br /> <br /> I\u2019m taking Coral Castle off this list. It\u2019s sad, not mysterious, occult or frightening. Beasts are about fear, not unrequited love.<br /> <br /> As for the earthworks of Newark...now <i>that</i> is interesting! Maybe Beasts of Native stock built them as physical extensions of their Lairs\u2014-perhaps to confuse Heroes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T06:50:10-07:00","id":1205177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1205156#post1205156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, i just read both articles, and...<br /> <br /> I\u2019m taking Coral Castle off this list. It\u2019s sad, not mysterious, occult or frightening. Beasts are about fear, not unrequited love.<br /> <br /> As for the earthworks of Newark...now <i>that</i> is interesting! Maybe Beasts of Native stock built them as physical extensions of their Lairs\u2014-perhaps to confuse Heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd write it as only some of them are that, with most being made by mortals and the initial idea being thought up by mortals but that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T06:55:22-07:00","id":1205178,"title":"","content":"They could also be built by any of the other supernatural splats for the crossover potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T07:22:49-07:00","id":1205189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1205178#post1205178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could also be built by any of the other supernatural splats for the crossover potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>...true. Beast <i>is</i> designed with crossover in mind!<br /> <br /> Hmmm...maybe, like all things, those earthworks\u2019re actually the conclusion of countless efforts\u2014-some mundane, some supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T07:34:38-07:00","id":1205196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1205189#post1205189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...true. Beast <i>is</i> designed with crossover in mind!<br /> <br /> Hmmm...maybe, like all things, those earthworks\u2019re actually the conclusion of countless efforts\u2014-some mundane, some supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neithian Architecture, Ley-line manipulation, Infrastructure, Shadow/Hedge/Underworld Gate creation or sealing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"us