link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T06:06:30-07:00","id":1205556,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, you could create your own city and take bits and pieces of the real world cities and shove them in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T15:15:56-07:00","id":1205776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1205556#post1205556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, you could create your own city and take bits and pieces of the real world cities and shove them in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. I\u2019d rather use a real city. It saves me a <i>ton</i> Of work, in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T15:43:11-07:00","id":1205792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1205776#post1205776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah. I\u2019d rather use a real city. It saves me a <i>ton</i> Of work, in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>You still <i>can</i>. Just like one could take Chicago, call it Gotham, and then only change what elements they need to.<br /> <br /> Take as much as you need to from an actual city (or cities), and just make note of where you deviate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T05:07:58-07:00","id":1214997,"title":"","content":"Ok, after doing some reading, I\u2019ve chosen Newark. Those earthenworks pose too many awesometastic possibilities, to pass up.<br /> <br /> In preparation, however, a small number of questions:<br /> 1.Is an Apex the most personally powerful supernatural in the area, the most influential, some combination of both?<br /> 2.Can some kind soul point me to online resources for Native American mythology and folktales, <i>especially</i> in the area of Newark?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T05:26:44-07:00","id":1215003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1214997#post1214997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, after doing some reading, I\u2019ve chosen Newark. Those earthenworks pose too many awesometastic possibilities, to pass up.<br /> <br /> In preparation, however, a small number of questions:<br /> 1.Is an Apex the most personally powerful supernatural in the area, the most influential, some combination of both?<br /> 2.Can some kind soul point me to online resources for Native American mythology and folktales, <i>especially</i> in the area of Newark?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about the Native American stuff, but for the Apex they're neither; they're the supernatural figure in the Hive's area who imposes the most fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T05:36:56-07:00","id":1215004,"title":"","content":"For a Native Apex (if it's a Beast, and not another figure), my go-to would probably be a form of the Horned Serpent: <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horned_Serpent\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Stati_uniti_o_messico%2C_casas_grandes%2C_giara_con_due_serpenti_piumati_e_cornuti%2C_uccelli_e_motivi_a_P%2C_new_mexico_o_chihuahua%2C_1280-1450_ca.jpg/1280px-Stati_uniti_o_messico%2C_casas_grandes%2C_giara_con_due_serpenti_piumati_e_cornuti%2C_uccelli_e_motivi_a_P%2C_new_mexico_o_chihuahua%2C_1280-1450_ca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horned_Serpent\" target=\"_blank\"> Horned Serpent - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horned_Serpent\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horned_Serpent </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The tribes in Newark (and in most of New-Jersey) belonged to the Algonquian group (Powhatan, Nanticoke, etc). I don't have any specific resource to propose you, but I'm sure that if you look it up, you'll find something.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T06:32:05-07:00","id":1215018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1215003#post1215003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about the Native American stuff, but for the Apex they're neither; they're the supernatural figure in the Hive's area who imposes the most fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is actually a little more than that, the book says that the apex is the strongest supernatural being in the hive area &lt;explicitly this, what it MEANS on the other hand...&gt;, but also says that one cannot be an apex if they don't interact with humanity regularly. So by proxy it will be the one who is the most feared; strong, and well known. On this &lt;as a side note, since I'm already talking about it&gt;, personally I would say that they could be &quot;defended&quot; by others who are less known, so they don't have to be the single strongest being, and still keep the title of Apex.<br /> <br /> How overthrowing works, on the other hand, I don't know, it just doesn't feel right that if you beat them in combat (and you qualify) you instantly become Apex, so I would say that &quot;fear&quot; or simply &quot;being known&quot; is the intended factor here. The book implies a challenge, but I think it isn't supposed to be physical. (between themselves, sure, but for the Hive, only their overall presence should matter) But if so, does this mean they don't have to meet at all?<br /> <br /> The whole emphasis on actually being the strongest just doesn't connect to the collective subconscious theme, but it is still in there. :/<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:06:35-07:00","id":1215061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1215018#post1215018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is actually a little more than that, the book says that the apex is the strongest supernatural being in the hive area &lt;explicitly this, what it MEANS on the other hand...&gt;, but also says that one cannot be an apex if they don't interact with humanity regularly. So by proxy it will be the one who is the most feared; strong, and well known.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lexicon says <i>most powerful <b>and feared</b></i>, for the record.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How overthrowing works, on the other hand, I don't know, it just doesn't feel right that if you beat them in combat (and you qualify) you instantly become Apex, so I would say that &quot;fear&quot; or simply &quot;being known&quot; is the intended factor here. The book implies a challenge, but I think it isn't supposed to be physical. (between themselves, sure, but for the Hive, only their overall presence should matter) But if so, does this mean they don't have to meet at all? </div> </div> </div>It's whatever supernatural creature has the greatest presence in the Primordial Dream through the formation of Chambers and similar thematic notes. For Beasts, this has a direct correlation with Lair; for other supernaturals, greater power tends to drive greater hunger, and feeding greater hunger tends to lead to greater influence on the Dream.<br /> <br /> Murder is a perennial favorite for supplanting the Apex, but otherwise I'd say it fits the tone for such a confrontation to end in a decisive victory for the would-be usurper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T09:29:28-07:00","id":1215101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1215004#post1215004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a Native Apex (if it's a Beast, and not another figure), my go-to would probably be a form of the Horned Serpent: <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horned_Serpent\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Stati_uniti_o_messico%2C_casas_grandes%2C_giara_con_due_serpenti_piumati_e_cornuti%2C_uccelli_e_motivi_a_P%2C_new_mexico_o_chihuahua%2C_1280-1450_ca.jpg/1280px-Stati_uniti_o_messico%2C_casas_grandes%2C_giara_con_due_serpenti_piumati_e_cornuti%2C_uccelli_e_motivi_a_P%2C_new_mexico_o_chihuahua%2C_1280-1450_ca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horned_Serpent\" target=\"_blank\"> Horned Serpent - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horned_Serpent\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horned_Serpent </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The tribes in Newark (and in most of New-Jersey) belonged to the Algonquian group (Powhatan, Nanticoke, etc). I don't have any specific resource to propose you, but I'm sure that if you look it up, you'll find something.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Uktena!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T10:15:18-07:00","id":1215133,"title":"","content":"I think a good barometer for the Apex is &quot;you better not mess with [X] in this town&quot;. Either explicitly or implicitly. If someone takes down [X], and this is known, they would tend to inherit the &quot;respect&quot; that was due to [X]. Depending on circumstances, of course. Sorry if this is vague, but I think the local circumstances really do play a large part of it.<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> If the Unholy (from Requiem) were staying in an area, they would probably be Apex (because they can rip apart whoever). If your PC took down the Unholy, then they would become Apex (because they dropped <i>the freaking Unholy</i>).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if the (pulled out of my head) Lord of Whispers was Apex because they knew <i>everything</i> about <i>everyone</i> in the area - where the bodies are buried, who you care about, etc. - then just being able to smash their face means nothing unless you also took them by surprise and/or swiped their information sources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-04-2018, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T10:30:16-07:00","id":1215138,"title":"","content":"That's pretty much what I had in mind as well, but what about this situation:<br /> <br /> In a small city, everyone is aware that a wolf hunts at night (werewolf), but in the town centre there is a well, where a witch (beast) dwells, and it is said that the wolf doesn't dare hunt there.<br /> <br /> So, this isn't true, the wolf hunts anywhere he pleases, but the two doesn't interfere with each other's business, no need.<br /> <br /> The well is more memorable, more people saw the witch overall. But the city has so many other places where the wolf was seen once or twice. And the werewolf is much stronger physically.<br /> <br /> Who is the apex?<br /> Is it the witch because people think she is?<br /> What happens if simply one day someone reports that the wolf attacked next to the well?<br /> Do they instantly switch Apex?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24132,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","user":"IceBen","date":". 05-04-2018, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T10:49:02-07:00","id":1215144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1215138#post1215138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's pretty much what I had in mind as well, but what about this situation:<br /> <br /> In a small city, everyone is aware that a wolf hunts at night (werewolf), but in the town centre there is a well, where a witch (beast) dwells, and it is said that the wolf doesn't dare hunt there.<br /> <br /> So, this isn't true, the wolf hunts anywhere he pleases, but the two doesn't interfere with each other's business, no need.<br /> <br /> The well is more memorable, more people saw the witch overall. But the city has so many other places where the wolf was seen once or twice. And the werewolf is much stronger physically.<br /> <br /> Who is the apex?<br /> Is it the witch because people think she is?<br /> What happens if simply one day someone reports that the wolf attacked next to the well?<br /> Do they instantly switch Apex?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple rumor isn't going to extend the witch's reach \u2014 the Apex may depend on how the locals think about their lives, but unless the witch is <i>scarier</i> and <i>has more frightening contact with humanity</i>, the witch isn't going to become the Apex just because her home is supposedly safe from the wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:08:53-07:00","id":1215156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1215138#post1215138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and it is said that the wolf doesn't dare hunt there</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what I mean by this, the people are convinced that the witch is stronger. She is indeed scarier and has more frightening contact with humanity, but ultimately weaker physically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:32:14-07:00","id":1215173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1215156#post1215156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She is indeed scarier and has more frightening contact with humanity, but ultimately weaker physically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does she have <i>more</i> frightening <i>contact</i> with humanity or more <i>frightening contact</i> with humanity? Because if more people <i>in the region</i> are afraid of the wolf then the town center is small potatoes \u2014 the witch's holdings and influence matter more than her having one Chamber the rumor mill says is above reproach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:48:39-07:00","id":1215181,"title":"","content":"Ok, some thoughts in my head, about this:<br /> 1.Though the other splats <i>will</i> be mentioned, this homebrew will focus virtually exclusively on Beasts and a single other splat, but which, I\u2019ve not yet decided on.<br /> 2.The Begotten are \u2018in control\u2019 in Newark, and, so, the Apex is a Beast.<br /> 3.The Hopewell earthworks will have a large part to play. Though these mounds were made by mundane humans, the Begotten made heavy use of them, too, giving them some sort of occult aspect, in the process. (Obcasus Rites, for the win!) Furthermore, some of these mounds will have a connection to the Insatiable, with the implication being used in twisted summoning-rites that called up the children of the Primogenitor...<br /> 4.Newark\u2019s Beasts will be going through a power struggle of some sort, most likely a Beast gunning for the position of Apex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 05-04-2018, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:53:59-07:00","id":1215185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1215173#post1215173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does she have <i>more</i> frightening <i>contact</i> with humanity or more <i>frightening contact</i> with humanity? Because if more people <i>in the region</i> are afraid of the wolf then the town center is small potatoes \u2014 the witch's holdings and influence matter more than her having one Chamber the rumor mill says is above reproach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both, she has more contact (more victims), and is scarier (more well known).<br /> The witch has created one chamber in the region, but keeps hunting there.<br /> The wolf created, lets say, eight, but doesn't focus on any of them, he hunts wherever.<br /> <br /> I don't know werewolf that much, so don't wanna say random things about how they hunt, but let's just say he chases and scares people, on occasions wounds them (no maimed corpses). While the witch does the same, but also makes people disappear (unknown what happens).<br /> <br /> So the witch is clearly the first target if hunters came to town. I hope this is enough explanation, because I intended to write just one sentence to represent this setup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:17:35-07:00","id":1215191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1215185#post1215185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both, she has more contact (more victims), and is scarier (more well known).<br /> The witch has created one chamber in the region, but keeps hunting there.<br /> The wolf created, lets say, eight, but doesn't focus on any of them, he hunts wherever.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the witch and the werewolf haven't come into direct conflict then it's going to come down to what the locals are like to determine whether a vicious monster that can strike anywhere is a bigger concern than a vicious monster that's set up camp in a central location.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I hope this is enough explanation, because I intended to write just one sentence to represent this setup. </div> </div> </div>When you throw a border case onto the pile it's going to require your own table's arbitration to settle no matter what, so asking for outside help is inherently going to require more than one sentence of detail \u2014 it's a storytelling game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:27:08-07:00","id":1215197,"title":"","content":"This isn't at my table, I'm asking you guys.<br /> <br /> But lets see like this:<br /> <br /> In a situation where A is physically stronger, but B is believed to be a bigger threat. Who is the Apex? I personally lean towards B, that's why I followed it with the questions I asked.<br /> Let's say B indeed is the Apex, then: if A proves he should be feared more, with a single random act, completely out of the blue, then does he instantly gain the title then and there? (Or do people need time to adjust)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:36:53-07:00","id":1215202,"title":"","content":"I find the title of Apex has to be maintained. It isn't a one time fight and then walk away with the title until the next challenge comes up. You build a legend, a nightmare, a terror of the town story, and you make sure it stays that way. If you get get killed, unless everyone know it, you are still warping the dream for a while. Heck, if a beast goes unfettered, the horror may keep it's comfy Apex spot. It could theoretically attach to another human, create another beast, and begin again, horror movie style.<br /> <br /> Once you beat the boss, you have to take his mantle. You may have the reigns for now, but if you don't keep up, don't be surprised when a newcomer suddenly overshadows your barely maintained legend.<br /> <br /> In a way, it's similar to a demons cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:37:41-07:00","id":1215204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1215197#post1215197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't at my table, I'm asking you guys.<br /> <br /> But lets see like this:<br /> <br /> In a situation where A is physically stronger, but B is believed to be a bigger threat. Who is the Apex? I personally lean towards B, that's why I followed it with the questions I asked.<br /> Let's say B indeed is the Apex, then: if A proves he should be feared more, with a single random act, completely out of the blue, then does he instantly gain the title then and there? (Or do people need time to adjust)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Primordial Dream is part of the Astral Realms, so, I\u2019d imagine perception can be just as important as reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:38:58-07:00","id":1215205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1215197#post1215197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't at my table, I'm asking you guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm telling you the answer to this question is going to depend on the table. This is not a question with a hard concrete answer, because it is a story-based thing in a game that is run by groups of individuals rather than an ingrained point of mechanical arbitration that anyone here is going to be able to tell you with more certainty than &quot;this is how I would run it in my game.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:46:50-07:00","id":1215208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1204985-i\u2019m-homebrewing-for-a-beast-campaign-and?p=1215197#post1215197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't at my table, I'm asking you guys.<br /> <br /> But lets see like this:<br /> <br /> In a situation where A is physically stronger, but B is believed to be a bigger threat. Who is the Apex? I personally lean towards B, that's why I followed it with the questions I asked.<br /> Let's say B indeed is the Apex, then: if A proves he should be feared more, with a single random act, completely out of the blue, then does he instantly gain the title then and there? (Or do people need time to adjust)</div> </div> </div> </div>A Might Prove to have a Reason to be feared, but if it's not something everyone (or atleast Enough) knows about... Then it wouldn't have an effect. Apexes &quot;Need&quot; to be known to maintain that title. Hence why if a Town has alot of Say Werewolves it's possible for one of them to be the Apex in the Hive without knowing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T13:19:08-07:00","id":1215215,"title":"","content":"Could a Beast form Kinship with an <i>idigam</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T13:20:56-07:00","id":1215217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-